From 57e78270cfe5a56739bd4f259b64f8d3f11fb7d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:38:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(blocks): render Bedrock state geometry and materials

Resolve custom block properties and ordered permutations after StartGame,
including per-face textures, geometry, transforms, shapes and lighting.
Reserve free note-block and redstone-wire states deterministically and deduplicate identical
visual and physical definitions. Preserve the original vanilla mapping
when a definition or a required custom texture cannot be represented.

Bedrock sends the runtime definitions after the initial pack. Keep Java
in configuration while it acknowledges a supplemental converted pack and
buffer ordered world packets with explicit count and byte bounds. Only
that pack's acknowledgement releases the scene; rejection clears custom
mappings before joining.

Saved Bedrock 1.26.51 scenes resolve all 276 CubeCraft states, all 1,795
Minehut states and all 199 Geyser states. Geyser mushroom faces use Java's corresponding vanilla
sprites when the server omits those vanilla Bedrock textures. Conversion
rejects ambiguous geometry and nonuniform scaling of rotated cubes. Legacy texture-array variation selection remains unimplemented.

Targeted tests cover permutations, transforms, face materials, lighting,
pack identity, rejection, queue bounds and one-shot completion.

Resume buffered packets with their Bedrock type after the base protocols that
already processed them. Preserve cancellation and downstream translation
without forcing either tracked connection state.

Bind the particle sprite explicitly for both full-cube and geometry block
models. The recorded Geyser scene exposed Java model warnings and missing
block particle textures despite valid face sprites.

Compose static parent-bone rotations child-to-root around their distinct
pivots and inflate cubes on both sides. Minehut's saved custom skulls need
these transforms and 1,790 distinct visuals, beyond the original 1,349
note-block carriers. Append 1,280 unoccupied, water-free wire states while
keeping note assignments stable and excluding every vanilla Bedrock
mapping. Preserve vanilla wire multipart selectors for unassigned states.
Native client adapters suppress carrier redstone particles and tint.

Exhaustive semantic tests cover all 1,296 wire states, exact custom/vanilla
partitions, compact selector conditions and ordinary note fallback.

Retain bone membership from the converter's remapped emitted group indices
when applying static block transforms. Invisible cubes emit no Java element
and must not shift later visible cubes into another bone. Regression
coverage combines invisible parent and child cubes with distinct rotated
bones, preserved face UVs, and immutable source geometry.
